<title>HONG KONG: Chow Sang Sang 1996 net down 41.7 pct.</title>
<headline>Chow Sang Sang 1996 net down 41.7 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	20.38    vs 34.95</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents) 14.0     vs 14.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items     nil	vs nil</p>
<p>    Net			 89.65    vs 153.79</p>
<p>    Turnover		  4,860.17 vs 6,114.60</p>
<p>    Company name	    Chow Sang Sang Holdings International</p>
<p>				  Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close	     June 20-26</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	July 4</p>
<p>NOTE - Chow Sang Sang engages in retailing, manufacturing, import and export of gold, jewellery and precious metals. It also has interests in gold trading and property investment.</p>
<p>Net is before an extraordinary item of HK$8.0 million loss represented an ex-gratia payment made to the families of staffs who died in the fire in the Garley Building vs nil.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is 21 H.K. cents (including interim dividend of seven cents) vs same.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
